Question: James decides to run 3 sprints 3 times a week.  He runs 60 meters each sprint.  How many total meters does he run a week?
Answer: **James runs 3 sprints per day (3 days/week), each lasting 60 meters.**

1. **Calculate Total Sprints Per Week:**
   \[
   \text{Total sprints} = 3 \text{ sprints/day} \times 3 \text{ days/week} = 9 \text{ sprints/week}
   \]

2. **Calculate Total Distance Run:**
   \[
   \text{Total distance} = \text{Number of sprints} \times \text{Distance per sprint} = 9 \text{ sprints} \times 60 \text{ meters/sprint} = 540 \text{ meters}
   \]

Thus, James runs \( \boxed{540} \) meters a week.<|im_end|>
