\[
\text{Number of teaspoons of sugar} = \frac{\text{Total sugar}}{\text{Ratio}} = \frac{120}{\frac{7}{13}}
\]

Perform the division:
\[
\frac{120}{\frac{7}{13}} = 120 \times \frac{13}{7}
\]
Simplify the fraction:
\[
120 \times \frac{13}{7} = 180
\]

Thus, the number of teaspoonfuls of sugar is:
