- Box B: \( 4 \times 0.40 = 1.67 \) black balls
- Box C: \( 6 \times 0.40 = 2.4 \) black balls

**Total Black Balls in Boxes A, B, and C:** 
\[ 2 + 1.67 + 2.4 = 6.07 \]

**Probability of picking all black balls from any single box:**
\[ P(A) = \frac{\text{Number of black balls in A}}{\text{Total black balls in A}} = \frac{2}{6.07} \approx 0.3189 \]

**Probability of drawing a white ball from any single box:**
\[ P(B) = \frac{\text{Number of white balls in B}}{\text{Total white balls in B}} = \frac{1.67}{6.07} \approx 0.2623 \]

**Combined Probability of both events happening:**

\[ P(A \cap B \cap W) = P(A) \times P(B) \]
\[ P(A \cap B \cap W) = 0.3189 \times 0.2623 \approx 0.0767 \]

Thus,
\[ p_1 + p_2 = 0.3189 + 0.2623 \approx 0.5812 \]

Therefore, \( p_1 + p_2 \) is:
\[ \boxed{0.5812} \]<|im_end|>
