     \frac{BC}{\sin(59.999^\circ)} > AB + \sin(60^\circ)
     \]

6. **Evaluate Specific Cases**:
    - If \( \sin(59.999^\circ) \approx 0.76 \), then:
      \[
      \frac{BC}{\sin(59.999^\circ)} > AB + \sin(60^\circ)
      \]
      Solving for \( n \):
      \[
      59.999 > AB + \sin(60^\circ)
      \]
      \[
      59.999 - \sin(60^\circ) > AB
      \]
      \[
      \sin(60^\circ) > AB - 59.999
      \]
      \[
      \sin(60^\circ) > 0.5 (since \sin(60^\circ) = 0.5)
      \]
      Therefore,
      \[
      0.5 > AB > 0
      \]
      Hence, \( n \geq 1 \).
  
Thus, the smallest \( n \) for which \(\triangle A_nB_nC_n\) is obtuse is:
\[
\boxed{1}
\]<|im_end|>
